The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'THELOOK_ECOMMERCE': {'THELOOK_ECOMMERCE': ['DISTRIBUTION_CENTERS', 'ORDERS', 'USERS', 'EVENTS', 'INVENTORY_ITEMS', 'PRODUCTS', 'ORDER_ITEMS']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns, their potential usage and possible conditions
• INVENTORY_ITEMS."sold_at":  identifies the moment an item was sold – filter to 2020 (`WHERE "sold_at" IS NOT NULL AND TO_TIMESTAMP("sold_at"/1e6) BETWEEN '2020‑01‑01' AND '2020‑12‑31'`).  
• INVENTORY_ITEMS."product_id":  joins to PRODUCTS to obtain attributes.  
• PRODUCTS."id":  primary key for the PRODUCTS table, join target.  
• PRODUCTS."name":  product description we finally need.  
• PRODUCTS."retail_price", PRODUCTS."cost":  used to calculate profit (`"retail_price"‑"cost"`).  
• Derived column `month_2020`:  `DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(i."sold_at"/1e6))` – lets us group by calendar month in 2020.  

10 exploration queries (Snowflake SQL)

```sql
--1. Inspect a few sale time‑stamps and product IDs
SELECT i."id", i."product_id", i."sold_at"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.INVENTORY_ITEMS i
WHERE i."sold_at" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--2. Convert micro‑seconds to a readable timestamp
SELECT i."id",
       i."product_id",
       TO_TIMESTAMP(i."sold_at"/1e6) AS "sold_ts"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.INVENTORY_ITEMS i
WHERE i."sold_at" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--3. Show sales that occurred only during 2020
SELECT i."id",
       i."product_id",
       TO_TIMESTAMP(i."sold_at"/1e6) AS "sold_ts"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.INVENTORY_ITEMS i
WHERE i."sold_at" IS NOT NULL
  AND TO_TIMESTAMP(i."sold_at"/1e6) BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--4. Bring in product names for 2020 sales
SELECT i."product_id",
       p."name",
       TO_TIMESTAMP(i."sold_at"/1e6) AS "sold_ts"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.INVENTORY_ITEMS i
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS p
  ON i."product_id" = p."id"
WHERE i."sold_at" IS NOT NULL
  AND TO_TIMESTAMP(i."sold_at"/1e6) BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--5. Calculate the profit (retail − cost) for each sold item in 2020
SELECT i."product_id",
       p."name",
       ROUND(p."retail_price" - p."cost",2) AS "profit",
       TO_TIMESTAMP(i."sold_at"/1e6) AS "sold_ts"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.INVENTORY_ITEMS i
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS p
  ON i."product_id" = p."id"
WHERE i."sold_at" IS NOT NULL
  AND TO_TIMESTAMP(i."sold_at"/1e6) BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--6. Bucket those sales by calendar month (2020 only)
SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(i."sold_at"/1e6)) AS "month_2020",
       i."product_id",
       p."name",
       ROUND(p."retail_price" - p."cost",2) AS "profit"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.INVENTORY_ITEMS i
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS p
  ON i."product_id" = p."id"
WHERE i."sold_at" IS NOT NULL
  AND TO_TIMESTAMP(i."sold_at"/1e6) BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--7. Observe the minimum profit achieved in each month
SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(i."sold_at"/1e6)) AS "month_2020",
       MIN(p."retail_price" - p."cost") AS "min_profit"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.INVENTORY_ITEMS i
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS p
  ON i."product_id" = p."id"
WHERE i."sold_at" IS NOT NULL
  AND TO_TIMESTAMP(i."sold_at"/1e6) BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--8. Attach each sale's profit and highlight the minimum per month
SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(i."sold_at"/1e6)) AS "month_2020",
       p."name",
       ROUND(p."retail_price" - p."cost",2) AS "profit",
       MIN(ROUND(p."retail_price" - p."cost",2)) 
           OVER (PARTITION BY DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(i."sold_at"/1e6))) AS "min_profit_same_month"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.INVENTORY_ITEMS i
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS p
  ON i."product_id" = p."id"
WHERE i."sold_at" IS NOT NULL
  AND TO_TIMESTAMP(i."sold_at"/1e6) BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
LIMIT 20;
```

